# PachaOS installed-base BusyBox init policy.
# Native seed0root owns hardware services; init owns the Linux user session.
# BusyBox init creates a new session for each action.  Its standard leading
# '-' form asks init to claim the inherited termd PTY as that session's
# controlling terminal before exec, preserving interactive job control.
::respawn:-/bin/ash
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/bin/sync
